# Response security headers for every path on the site.
#
# Scope is the subset that cannot break ad delivery or analytics:
#   - frame-ancestors 'self' / X-Frame-Options: who may frame US (clickjacking).
#     It does not restrict the ad iframes we embed, so AdSense/Monetag are unaffected.
#   - object-src 'none', base-uri 'self', form-action 'self': plugin content,
#     <base> injection, form hijack. No page posts to a third-party origin
#     (verified against live HTML).
#   - upgrade-insecure-requests: every asset is already https.
# A full content CSP (script-src/style-src/connect-src allowlist) is deliberately
# NOT set: the ad network rotates hosts at runtime (Monetag loaded from 6opo.com
# while its tag domain is quge5.com; AdSense pulls ep2.adtrafficquality.google),
# so an enforced allowlist silently kills ad revenue. Verified host inventory for a
# future rollout: docs/security-headers.md.
# HSTS is set by the zone-level header rule, not here (one owner per header).
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Content-Security-Policy: object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests

/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
